cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PsyRAT: The Psychophysiologist's Reliability Analysis Toolbox"
message: >-
  If you use this toolbox, we recommend citing Rocha et al. (2026), the source
  of the reliability formulas (listed first under references), together with
  the GitHub release of the toolbox version you ran. The version string from
  psyrat_defineversion (printed in the startup banner and written into every
  exported table header and *_runconfig.json sidecar) identifies that release.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Clayson
    given-names: Peter E.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4437-6598"
version: 0.1.0-beta
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/peclayson/PsyRAT"
abstract: >-
  A MATLAB toolbox that uses generalizability theory to evaluate the
  psychometric reliability of event-related potential (ERP) scores.
  Variance components are estimated in a Bayesian framework via CmdStan.
  The toolbox reports dependability (absolute-error) and generalizability
  (relative-error) coefficients for designs with any number of events,
  groups, or occasions; estimates the effect of trial count on dependability
  and recommends a trial-count cutoff for inclusion; and estimates the
  internal consistency of difference scores.
keywords:
  - generalizability theory
  - reliability
  - dependability
  - event-related potentials
  - ERP
  - psychometrics
  - psychophysiology
  - Bayesian estimation
  - Stan

# No preferred-citation block on purpose: in CFF 1.2.0 that key tells citation
# tooling (GitHub's "Cite this repository", cffconvert) to emit the named work
# INSTEAD of the software, which defeats the recommendation in message. Rocha
# et al. (2026) is listed first under references because it is the source of
# the formulas the toolbox implements: its Tables 2, 3 and 6 give the one-facet
# G/D/ICC/SEM, test-retest, and difference-score expressions.
#
# TO REVISIT: a dedicated PsyRAT software/methods publication is planned. When
# it is released, add it here and reconsider a preferred-citation block then.
references:
  # The source of the reliability formulas (Tables 2, 3 and 6);
  # PsyRATIndependentOracle states those tables in the paper's own symbols as
  # the suite's external corroboration.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Beyond classical metrics: Generalizability theory across
      psychophysiological modalities
    authors:
      - family-names: Rocha
        given-names: Harold A.
      - family-names: Holbrook
        given-names: Amanda
      - family-names: Hajcak
        given-names: Greg
      - family-names: Keil
        given-names: Andreas
      - family-names: Rast
        given-names: Philippe
      - family-names: Thayer
        given-names: Julian F.
      - family-names: Verona
        given-names: Edelyn
      - family-names: Vispoel
        given-names: Walter P.
      - family-names: Clayson
        given-names: Peter E.
    journal: "International Journal of Psychophysiology"
    volume: 222
    number: 113321
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.1016/j.ijpsycho.2026.113321"

  # The location-scale / Bayesian variance-component basis for the estimation
  # core. Accepted 9 December 2025; no volume or issue has been assigned, so it
  # is cited in press rather than by year.
  - type: article
    title: >-
      Enhancing generalizability theory with mixed-effects models for
      heteroscedasticity in psychological measurement: A theoretical
      introduction with an application from EEG data
    authors:
      - family-names: Rast
        given-names: Philippe
      - family-names: Clayson
        given-names: Peter E.
    journal: "British Journal of Mathematical and Statistical Psychology"
    status: in-press
    doi: "10.1111/bmsp.70026"

  - type: article
    title: >-
      Using generalizability theory and the ERP Reliability Analysis (ERA)
      Toolbox for assessing test-retest reliability of ERP scores part 1:
      Algorithms, framework, and implementation
    authors:
      - family-names: Clayson
        given-names: Peter E.
      - family-names: Carbine
        given-names: Kaylie A.
      - family-names: Baldwin
        given-names: Scott A.
      - family-names: Olsen
        given-names: Joseph A.
      - family-names: Larson
        given-names: Michael J.
    journal: "International Journal of Psychophysiology"
    volume: 166
    start: 174
    end: 187
    year: 2021
    doi: "10.1016/j.ijpsycho.2021.01.006"
